assistant: Subject: follow next_cursor when paging product search results

Root cause: `search_products` made one `GET /products?q=` call and returned only that page. Vendor version 2026-10-01 now splits results into pages: it sent 5 of 7 matches with `next_cursor: "5"`, and the tool ignored the cursor (the spec does document it), so it returned an incomplete list. The fix keeps fetching `&cursor=<next_cursor>` and adding each page's items until `next_cursor` is null or missing. In the v1 fixtures `next_cursor` is null, so v1 still sends the same single request and gives the same output. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass. I didn't touch a second problem the alert also raised: v2 prices come back about 100× the v1 values (p-1101 is 6900, was 69), probably cents. The spec's "Unit price" says nothing about units and the response has no unit field, so dividing by 100 would be a guess. Someone should confirm the unit with the vendor before changing it, and the same fix would likely be needed in `get_product`.

